{
 "id": "page-releve-science",
 "target": "page",
 "page": "releve.html",
 "goal": "Record a sagebrush-steppe releve whole and hold what the sheet computes. Three taxa by Braun-Blanquet class -- big sagebrush 4 (midpoint 62.5%), bluebunch wheatgrass 2 (15%), cheatgrass + (0.5%) -- read 3 taxa in 2 families, Shannon H' 0.53, evenness J' 0.48, 1.7 effective taxa, one non-native and the dominant at 80% of recorded cover, with 80% of that cover shrub; a fourth taxon at class 1 moves them to 0.67, 0.48, 1.9 and 77%, and an add with no cover class adds no row. Floristic Quality Assessment over two of three natives is mean C 4.50, FQI 6.4, adjusted FQI 31.8 and says so is partial; over three of three it is 4.33, 7.5 and 37.5. Scored UPL/FACU the Corps prevalence index is 4.77, above the 3.0 threshold, and the sheet says a determination still needs hydric soil and hydrology. A 50 m transect read at 1 m in duplicate plans 100 points and at 0.5 m plans 200; five top-canopy hits and four bare readings on the 100-point denominator are 5% foliar cover and 4% bare with 91 points still to read. A 40.5853/-111.6383 fix with 30 m of GPS on a 100 m2 plot is 43 m of coordinate uncertainty -- 7 m of it the plot itself -- and 5402 m with the datum unknown. A pack missing its required fields is rejected whole.",
 "policy": {
  "allow": [
   "SENSITIVE_READ",
   "DRAFT",
   "MUTATE",
   "DESTRUCTIVE"
  ],
  "needs": [
   "undo"
  ],
  "why": "the goal includes undoing the last line-point hit: lUndo is 'Undo'"
 },
